{title: Aura Lee}
{artist: W. W. Fosdick (words), George R. Poulton (music)}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}
{meta: public_domain Words by W. W. Fosdick, music by George R. Poulton; published 1861.}
{meta: source Sheet music "Aura Lea", Cincinnati, 1861.}
{meta: arrangement Original chord arrangement for Fretlight}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
As the [C]blackbird in the [D7]spring,
'Neath the [G7]willow [C]tree,
Sat and [C]piped, I heard him [D7]sing,
Sing of [G7]Aura [C]Lee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Aura [E7]Lee, [Am]Aura [C7]Lee,
[F]Maid of [C]golden hair,
[C]Sunshine [D7]came a[G7]long with [C]thee,
And [G7]swallows in the [C]air.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
In thy [C]blush the rose was [D7]born,
Music [G7]when you [C]spake,
Through thine [C]azure eye the [D7]morn,
Sparkling, [G7]seemed to [C]break.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
